      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017. Published by Elsevier Inc.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "AIMS",
            "content": "MicroRNA served as inhibitor for gene expression in various cancers. This study aimed to investigate the role of miR-605 and EN2 in prostate cancer (PCa)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "MATERIALS AND METHODS",
            "content": "In this research, the expression of miR-605 and EN2 protein in PCa tissues and cells were determined by qRT-PCR and western blot, respectively. The cell proliferation was measured by Cell Counting Kit-8 (CCK-8) and the tumor cell invasion assay was accomplished with transwell system. Flow cytometry was used to analyze the cell cycle. The endogenous expression of miR-605 and EN2 was modulated by recombinant plasmids and cell transfection. Dual luciferase reporter assay was performed to determine the interaction between miR-605 and EN2 in PCa cells."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "KEY FINDINGS",
            "content": "The expression of miR-605 was lower in PCa tissue and cells than that in normal tissues and cells, while the expression of EN2 was just the opposite. Down-regulation of the EN2 by siRNA inhibited the proliferation and invasion of PC3 cells, and the cell cycle was arrested in G0/G1 phase. EN2 regulated the expression of E-cadherin and Vimentin through Snail and EN2 regulated the cell cycle and cell proliferation via PI3K/AKT pathway. MiR-605 inhibited the proliferation and invasion of PCa cells through targeting EN2."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "SIGNIFICANCE",
            "content": "EN2 is negatively regulated by miR-605, and down-regulation of miR-605 promotes the proliferation and invasion of PCa cells by up-regulating EN2, which leads to PCa development and progression."
          }
        ]
      },
